  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kansas federal contract obligations are $130M in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 2,770 awards with an average award size of $47K. Contract obligations are down 96.6% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows a steep drop from earlier totals: FY22 was $4.3B, FY23 was $3.1B, FY24 was $3.4B, FY25 was $3.7B, and FY26 was $3.8B. The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying in FY2027 to date with $54.5M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $49.8M. CORE CIVIC, INC. is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $49.8M, and FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION is second with $19.9M. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date at $50.4M, with Couriers and Express Delivery Services next at $19.9M. These figures are fiscal year to date and partial for the current year. The snapshot shows a concentration of obligations in a few agencies, vendors, and industries during the FY2027-to-date reporting period.",
