        "heading": "How much federal contracting activity is Kansas seeing this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Kansas federal contract obligations are $130M in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 2,770 awards with an average award size of $47K. Obligations are down 96.6% year over year compared with prior full-year totals. Fiscal-year history shows much larger totals in earlier years, including $3.8B in FY26 and $4.3B in FY22."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate Kansas obligations right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying with $54.5M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $49.8M. CORE CIVIC, INC. is the top vendor at $49.8M and FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION is next at $19.9M. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the top industry at $50.4M, with Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $19.9M."
      }
